@startuml
!theme plain
title Promo codes · Manager management and customer validation
autonumber
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true

actor "Manager" as MG
actor "Customer" as U
participant "Frontend" as F
participant "NestJS API" as A
database "PostgreSQL" as DB

== Management ==
MG -> F : Creates a promo code
F -> A : POST /promo-codes
activate A
alt Not a manager
  A --> F : 403 Forbidden
else The code already exists
  A --> F : 409 Conflict
else Success
  A -> DB : Inserts with its discount, validity window and usage cap
  A --> F : 201
end
deactivate A
F -> A : GET /promo-codes
A --> F : 200, including expired and exhausted ones
F -> A : PATCH /promo-codes/ID
note right of A : Validity window or cap gets adjusted. The code itself\nisn't rewritten: it's already in people's hands

== Validation before paying ==
U -> F : Enters the promo code in the cart
F -> A : POST /promo-codes/validate\ncode + the current cart
activate A
alt Doesn't exist, expired or exhausted
  A --> F : 404 or 409
  F -> U : That code doesn't work
else The cart doesn't reach the minimum
  A --> F : 409 Conflict
else The discounted total would fall below the chargeable minimum
  A --> F : 409 Conflict
  note right of A : Stripe won't charge below its minimum.\nBetter to say so here than fail at checkout
else Applies
  A --> F : 200 with the discount and the resulting total
  F -> U : Shows the discounted total
end
deactivate A

note over F, A #ffe0e0
  Validating holds **nothing**. A usage is held in
  POST /orders, alongside the stock hold, and is released when the
  order is paid, cancelled or expires. Between validation and
  checkout the last use may have been taken by someone else: that's
  why checkout re-checks it and may respond 409 for the coupon.
end note

@enduml
